 "description": "/ Psychology vs AI",
 "body_html": "<p>Dr. Dario Krpan is an Associate Professor of Behavioural Science at London School of Economics. His research focuses on social and cognitive psychology, and behavioural change in response to new technology.</p><p>He recently published <a href=\"https://journals.sagepub.com/doi/10.1177/10892680261470738\">From Nexus to the Tower of Babel: On Truly Human Psychology in the Dawn of AI</a>, and agreed to speak to me about it.  I recommend you check out the full paper this weekend. </p><p><em>(I\u2019m trying to get more used to recording myself, still not used to it, but striving to improve)</em></p><p><strong>Timestamps:</strong></p><p>0:00 Stefan and Dario say hi</p><p>4:55 Extreme progress and Einstein-level ideas</p><p><strong>9:00 The Nexus and Babel metaphor</strong></p><p><strong>11:20 Dario lays out full argument for psychology\u2019s future</strong></p><p>19:45 Iain McGilchrist and the hemispheres</p><p>23:30 Humans aren\u2019t constant</p><p>25:45 Mathematics is well-scoped in a way Psychology is not</p><p>26:45 Nexus isn\u2019t necessarily a route to a complete Psychology anyway</p><p>29:40 History in social science is written by the winners</p><p>33:10 Positivism vs the inner world as source of data</p><p>39:45 Scientific truth always ends up at personal truth</p><p>40:45 Mechanistic viewpoints lead to mechanistic societies</p><p>45:30 Finding more inspiration from older Psychology writing</p><p>50:40 What if AI starts understanding things that we don\u2019t?</p><p>56:00 Collective Unconscious, Ingressing Minds, Morphogenic Spaces</p><p>1:02:15 What Psychologists are going to as AI gets better </p><p></p><p><strong>Links to things mentioned in order:</strong></p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://sites.pitt.edu/~jdnorton/Goodies/Einstein_think/index.html\">Einstein on his thought processes</a></p></li><li><p><a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1177/10892680261470738\">From Nexus to the Tower of Babel: On Truly Human Psychology in the Dawn of AI \u2014 Dario Krpan</a></p></li><li><p><a href=\"https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Genesis+11%3A1-9&amp;version=NIV\">The Tower of Babel \u2014 Genesis 11</a></p></li><li><p><a href=\"https://deepmind.google/science/alphafold/\">AlphaFold</a></p></li><li><p><a href=\"https://www.rizzoliusa.com/book/9780847871049/\">Codex Seraphinianus \u2014 Luigi Serafini</a></p></li><li><p><a href=\"https://beinecke.library.yale.edu/beinecke/collections/beinecke-cipher-voynich-manuscript\">The Voynich Manuscript</a></p></li><li><p><a href=\"https://www.penguinrandomhouse.com/books/321920/finnegans-wake-by-james-joyce/\">Finnegans Wake \u2014 James Joyce</a></p></li><li><p><a href=\"https://www.penguinrandomhouse.com/books/288210/the-tibetan-book-of-the-dead-by-gyurme-dorje/\">The Tibetan Book of the Dead</a></p></li><li><p><a href=\"https://channelmcgilchrist.com/master-and-his-emissary/\">The Master and His Emissary \u2014 Iain McGilchrist</a></p></li><li><p><a href=\"https://channelmcgilchrist.com/matter-with-things/\">The Matter with Things \u2014 Iain McGilchrist</a></p></li><li><p><a href=\"https://wwnorton.co.uk/books/9780393065671-the-red-book\">The Red Book \u2014 C. G. Jung</a></p></li><li><p><a href=\"https://philemonfoundation.org/works/black-books/\">The Black Books \u2014 C. G. Jung</a></p></li><li><p><a href=\"https://www.versobooks.com/blogs/authors/feyerabend-paul\">Paul Feyerabend</a></p></li><li><p><a href=\"https://www.penguinrandomhouse.com/books/323289/religions-values-and-peak-experiences-by-abraham-h-maslow/\">Religions, Values, and Peak-Experiences \u2014 Abraham Maslow</a></p></li><li><p><a href=\"https://www.rollomay.net/about-rollo-may/\">Rollo May</a></p></li><li><p><a href=\"https://www.julianjaynes.org/book/ooc/en/\">The Origin of Consciousness in the Breakdown of the Bicameral Mind \u2014 Julian Jaynes</a></p></li><li><p><a href=\"https://store.steampowered.com/app/3097560/Liars_Bar/\">Liar\u2019s Bar</a></p></li><li><p><a href=\"https://www.dogsplayingpoker.org/gallery/coolidge/\">Dogs Playing Poker \u2014 Cassius Marcellus Coolidge</a></p></li><li><p><a href=\"https://www.mdpi.com/2409-9287/11/5/161\">Ingressing Minds: Causal, Non-Physical Patterns In-Form Natural, Synthetic, and Hybrid Embodiments \u2014 Michael Levin</a></p></li><li><p><a href=\"https://www.sheldrake.org/research/morphic-resonance\">Morphic Resonance \u2014 Rupert Sheldrake</a></p></li><li><p><a href=\"https://www.seti.org/research/seti-101/fermi-paradox\">The Fermi Paradox</a></p></li><li><p><a href=\"https://adsabs.harvard.edu/pdf/1964SvA.....8..217K\">Transmission of Information by Extraterrestrial Civilizations \u2014 Nikolai Kardashev</a></p></li><li><p><a href=\"https://profiles.ucsf.edu/robin.carhart-harris\">Robin Carhart-Harris</a></p></li><li><p><a href=\"https://doi.org/10.31234/osf.io/8qvgy_v2\">Traces of the Other: Are DMT Entities Real? \u2014 Andrew Gallimore, Niffe Hermansson and Donald Hoffman</a></p></li><li><p><a href=\"https://christofkoch.com/\">Christof Koch</a></p></li><li><p><a href=\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3909994/\">The Entropic Brain: A Theory of Conscious States Informed by Neuroimaging Research with Psychedelic Drugs</a></p></li></ul><p></p><div class=\"subscription-widget-wrap-editor\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://www.alreadyhappened.xyz/subscribe?&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Subscribe&quot;,&quot;language&quot;:&quot;en&quot;}\" data-component-name=\"SubscribeWidgetToDOM\"><div class=\"subscription-widget show-subscribe\"><div class=\"preamble\"><p class=\"cta-caption\">Already Happened is a reader-supported publication. To receive new posts and support my work, consider becoming a free or paid subscriber.</p></div><form class=\"subscription-widget-subscribe\"><input type=\"email\" class=\"email-input\" name=\"email\" placeholder=\"Type your email\u2026\" tabindex=\"-1\"><input type=\"submit\" class=\"button primary\" value=\"Subscribe\"><div class=\"fake-input-wrapper\"><div class=\"fake-input\"></div><div class=\"fake-button\"></div></div></form></div></div><p></p>",
